{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgHxckpHV6rLhXnN8cwQE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, `sync.sh` rewrites `tracker.json` every hour when cron runs it. The test reads whatever file is there when it runs, so it does not depend on the count being 3.\n\n**Tomorrow, if the file is valid and has the same shape, the test passes.** If the open count changes from 3 to 5, both `weekly_report()` and the test's own count change with it.\n\nThe test can still break in these cases:\n\n- **The file is missing or invalid JSON.** If a sync fails midway, the test errors. That is a real signal, but it is not a count mismatch.\n- **The export changes its state values.** If the tracker starts writing `\"Open\"` or `\"in_progress\"`, `open_count` and the test both miscount in the same way, so the test still passes while the report is wrong. The test checks that the report agrees with the rule. It does not check the rule.\n- **The test reads during a rewrite.** If it opens the file while the sync is writing, it may read a partial file. Rare, but possible.\n\nThe check that catches the state-value problem is a fixed fixture with known open and closed issues. That test would not depend on the live export. I can add one if you want it. It would sit next to this test, which checks the live file.\n\nI also checked `sync.sh` in this copy. It does not sync anything. It prints `sync: no tracker configured in this copy` and exits. So nothing here rewrites `tracker.json`. The hourly rewrite happens only where cron runs the real script."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":380,"cache_read_input_tokens":43023,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":380},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"